WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:05.920
This yarn might not make the best sweater,

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:11.580
An international team of researchers

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:12.920
“Twistron harvesters.”

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.920
These tiny twists consist of a carbon nanotube string,

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.460
tied into a tangled weave of carbon,

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:21.400
then submerged in a gel full of ions

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:22.200
When pulled,

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.560
carbon nanotubes squeeze together,

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.860
decreasing the electrochemical capacitance,

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.580
and thereby generating a small current.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.460
Enough to momentarily light up an LED.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.800
Previously, capacitance-change-based

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.280
mechanical energy harvesters needed

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.740
external voltage to generate electricity

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:42.780
But now, this research shows that carbon nanotubes

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.480
can produce electricity just as well,

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.280
without the extra juice.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.740
The researchers tested the carbon nanotube
yarn’s

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:53.300
power-generating ability in several situations.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.980
This shirt has a pair of these Twistron yarns sewn in.

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:58.640
When the wearer breathes in and out,

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:00.940
a small amount of electricity is generated,

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:03.960
which could be useful data for medical devices.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.280
Researchers also looked into whether this
tech

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:08.860
could harness power from ocean waves.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:09.780
The harvesters worked

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:11.680
when placed in ocean-like saltwater,

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:13.340
and were able to generate electricity

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:16.180
when the wave motion tugged on the yarn.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:18.140
More power can be generated if the harvesters

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:20.920
are hooked up together, with peak power generation

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:23.599
reaching 250 Watts per kilogram.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:25.680
While these proof of concepts don’t generate

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:26.940
enough power to light your home or

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:28.940
charge your electric car,

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:31.360
the researchers say that due to their scalable nature,

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:34.500
these carbon nanotube yarns may have applications

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:37.520
anywhere reliable kinetic energy is available.

